sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Queue@{ "type": "queue" } as Redis and Celery queue
    participant Audio@{ "type": "control" } as Audio worker
    participant FFmpeg@{ "type": "entity" } as FFmpeg
    participant FileStore@{ "type": "database" } as File-linked object storage
    participant DB@{ "type": "database" } as PostgreSQL
    participant Backend@{ "type": "control" } as Backend worker
    participant Summary@{ "type": "boundary" } as Summary service

    Queue->>Audio: extract_audio(file_id)<br/>queue: dictaphone-audio
    Audio->>DB: Claim pending audio extraction
    Audio->>FileStore: Read source object using persisted file storage
    Audio->>FFmpeg: Run ffmpeg to extract and normalize audio

    alt Audio extraction failure
        FFmpeg-->>Audio: Extraction failure
        Audio->>FileStore: Delete partial derived audio
        Audio->>DB: Mark AUDIO_EXTRACTION_FAILED
    else Audio extraction succeeds
        FFmpeg-->>Audio: Normalized OGG/Opus audio and duration
        Audio->>FileStore: Write derived audio object
        Audio->>DB: Mark EXTRACTION_DONE and save duration
        Audio->>Queue: call_transcribe_service.delay(file_id)<br/>queue: dictaphone-backend
        Queue->>Backend: call_transcribe_service(file_id)<br/>queue: dictaphone-backend
        Backend->>DB: Create PENDING transcription job
        Backend->>FileStore: Generate signed GET URL for derived audio
        Backend->>Summary: POST /api/v2/async-jobs/transcribe

        alt Transcription request failure
            Summary-->>Backend: Request failure
            Backend->>DB: Mark transcription job FAILED
        else Transcription request succeeds
            Summary-->>Backend: 200 pending and remote job id
            Backend->>DB: Save remote transcription job id
        end
    end

    Note over Audio,FileStore: Every storage operation here uses the storage configuration persisted on the file.
